# Enforce Unix LF line endings for shell scripts
*.sh text eol=lf

# Line endings: DELIBERATELY not normalized here.
#
# The repo stores a mix (measured 2026-09-20: 52 CRLF blobs against 146 LF in
# a 200-file sample of *.py). That is why a tool which rewrites a whole file
# on Windows can turn a 50-line fix into a 669-line diff — the blob flips and
# every line reads as changed.
#
# `* text=auto` is the correct long-term fix and was tried. It was reverted:
# attributes OVERRIDE core.autocrlf, so the first `git add` of each legacy
# CRLF-blob file normalizes it and produces one whole-file diff apiece. A
# 67-line CHANGELOG entry came out as 15,987 insertions. Landing that ahead of
# a code freeze pays the entire cost up front and collects the benefit — clean
# diffs on future edits — only if there are future edits.
#
# When active development resumes, do it properly and in ONE commit:
#     echo '* text=auto' >> .gitattributes
#     git add --renormalize .      # ~257 files, ~70k lines, endings only
#     git commit -m 'chore: normalize line endings'
# Doing it as a single deliberate commit is reviewable ("endings only");
# doing it incidentally, a file at a time, is not.

# Binary — never convert. No churn: these were never being converted.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.db binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
